{"findings":[{"rule":"J3","where":"Deployment._configureModules (override of BaseSetup._configureModules)","severity":"HIGH","why":"The override only calls _setCap(CAP) and drops the base calls to _restrictCountry(RESTRICTED). The country module is bound to the compliance contract, but country 408 is never added, so the restriction does nothing.","steps":"Deploy with the override; countryModule.isCountryRestricted(compliance, 408) returns false; every moduleCheck in the country module passes."}
,{"rule":"J1","where":"Deployment._configureModules / CountryRestrictModule.moduleCheck","severity":"HIGH","why":"Wallet c is registered with country 408 and holds a valid KYC claim. Because 408 is not in the restricted set, c passes both isVerified and canTransfer and can receive tokens.","steps":"agent calls token.mint(c, 100) and it succeeds; b calls token.transfer(c, 10) and it succeeds."}
,{"rule":"J2","where":"Deployment._configureModules / IdentityRegistry.updateCountry","severity":"HIGH","why":"Updating a wallet's country to 408 has no effect on its ability to receive, because the country module has no restricted countries configured.","steps":"agent calls ir.updateCountry(b, 408); a1 calls token.transfer(b, 10) and it succeeds."}]}
